{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner completed R4's main-note and invariant-catalogue reading at exact2f83bf8c75c7fec706cd2310eeef5c986da0e2bb, under requestb18554a6/promisef3c5d607. Main564 lines39613 bytes,SHA-256f716efa35eda24394ff38f6ec8187f59b98a98dff4e406e10239ff2908b91aff; catalogue87 lines11182 bytes,SHA-25610d256a01fd14356e0181435c8dab26013ed5e81336d434744ae6afc31beb8fa. Both read in full; the five-file design-only diff whitespace check passed. All5 source-file byte/line/SHA identities were computed. This is not a completed per-test audit review. Of the git/mcp/cli/ui audit I read lines1-110 and950-1075 only; the middle and both other audits remain owed. I also read complete docs/testing.md atd691 and bounded actual source bodies in first-commit.test.ts:1-115, treediff.test.ts:148-192, gitops.test.ts:72-156. No test or provider action was run.\n\nSeven main/catalogue and sampled-audit corrections can proceed now, while the remaining complete row reading continues. These are internal design findings, not independent approval, permission to remove tests, a measured performance result or source commissioning.\n\n1. Update the baseline contracts coherently. The main says R1rev3/R2rev2/R3draft1; the catalogue still calls lost delivery permanently undeliverable, says a complete inventory settles unknown effects (A10), and assigns a fork per commitment (A11). Carry current R1rev4+full errata, R2rev3 and correctionddd83f7e, and R3rev3 at45727248 (announced27b2fa7e, bytes not yet read here) with current corrections5fd10474. Preserve unknown prior sends/mints, exact responder/operation correlation, complete eligibility, per-hold/instance custody and explicit grace. Replace blanket O1 'malformed input is retryable' with separate permanent malformed refusal/report versus evaluation/host failure that recorded no act. O3 must allow intentionally protected credential custody while excluding secrets from public records/errors/logs; O8 needs an exact semantic-byte/projection rule, not an unexplained equivalence of meaning. Label named operational assumptions honestly.\n\n2. Reduce the host witness overhead. Section7 proposes N=2,5,10 for20 rounds each,50 reads and an extra two-ref fault despite the design not using a two-ref transaction. That is a multiplied repetition plan inconsistent with the compact distinct-invariant rule. Use a small named set covering the actual compare-and-swap competition, original-versus-fence orders, delayed unknown send, lost reply, read route and create-only receipt/late retry. Reuse valid immutable historical evidence only with its exact boundary qualified. Repeated observations may estimate a specific stated rate, but cannot turn finite successes into a universal H1/H2 guarantee. Omit the unused two-ref experiment unless it answers a current design dependency. Keep owned resource/credential cleanup and uncertain effects accounted, and budget cost before any separately commissioned run. This adds no provider or Jam ceremony and authorizes no probe now.\n\n3. Make acceptance coverage inspectable and reconcile faults. Section6's ten variants currently list boundary/owner/brief note, without exact invariant clause, injection, expected result and retained evidence. Trace every R0 functional variant to those details, preserving complete checkpoint bytes/Git closure/guarded receipt, same-instance stale callbacks, detached writers, unknown external commands, failed saves/deletes, device-B private access and actual fork/credential fencing. Keep staged C2 storage/process proof distinct from integrated authority proof. Define the exact nine additional race rows rather than a count. F13 must distinguish missing source bytes from hash corruption or a valid source with no matching send; compare the actual new replay report categories and never call contradiction merely a missing dependency. Do not use B3 tests against task scopes that exist only at B7 in the graph; give the real local task platform object a fixture, while qualifying scripted runtime controls. Keep one deployed full journey, not a repetition per fault. A non-code result with no commit must agree with R2/R3's optional report fields and conditional staging, not force code work into every lane.\n\n4. Make row classifications semantic rather than title-based. In the first110 audit lines, Retain includes treediff.test.ts:169's old previewPlan decision and gitops.test.ts:77's old lane/generation preview API, although the new integration is assembled explicitly and those mechanisms are not automatically carried. More decisively first-commit.test.ts:80 is marked Retain under A13: I read its complete body and it classifies200 empty/incomplete replies (and generic401) as refused. A13's new contract requires unknown whenever an update may have been sent; the fake reply does not prove no creation. Rewrite the useful no-false-success/no-secret invariant at the new uncertainty boundary, with the exact evidence distinguishing refusal, not-sent and unknown, instead of porting that assertion. Recheck the retained rows' bodies and exports against the kept module's actual new role; consolidate redundant earlier tests into compact clause witnesses. A key or a surviving module name alone does not prove useful invariant coverage. Retain semantic invariants, not historical mechanism/API constraints.\n\n5. Reconcile the audit population and provenance. Section9 says1879 rows are behind the2053-case gate, but this audit explicitly includes UI Playwright rows outside the gate; its final notes acknowledge CLI/UI source-versus-recorded count differences. Partition source declarations, expanded cases, runner-discovered gate cases, skipped/duplicate-runtime cases and outside-gate browser cases at exactd691. Account for each difference rather than using one count for all. The audits cite r4-invariants.md/r4-audit-rules.md that are not the delivered paths; include their exact immutable provenance or fix the links. The row-declaration checker must cover suites/loops/parameterized declarations without treating a regex census as executed discovery; retain the checking method/input identity. Reconcile closing unkeyed operational-invariant lists and main counts, so a row initially marked Remove but later reassigned O1-O16 has one unambiguous proposed disposition. Later source-repair/new-test deltas need individual final-audit accounting rather than being silently excluded by the old baseline. Whole remaining audit reading is still owed here.\n\n6. Measure the full economy and all bounds. Keep elapsed and CPU, cold install/setup as well as valid warm-cache gates, edit-to-answer and reviewer/real-boundary costs. Root-only30s and a partial first I1 delivery cannot demonstrate10x for the whole final system. State the paired comparison to the earlier reference path and qualify differences in machine/load/cache/workload; include required browser/application and moved-package validation costs rather than hiding them outside the root gate. Gate once per actual relevant head, no runtime gate for unchanged source/tests, focused distinct witnesses and no mutation quota remain correct. Record how a fresh checkout proves dependencies installed; 'lock unchanged' alone is insufficient. Workload proposed budgets and approved operational limits are separate: observation grace/retention/expiry cannot be chosen just from cost, and product safety semantics must be explicit before testing. Include actual list/slot/record limits from R2's full definitions, settlement reserve/backpressure capacity under outstanding duties, overflow and incomplete export. A hot script that merely fails to reach5000 comments does not prove overflow handling. Do not drop functional witnesses or reset outstanding duties to meet a ceiling.\n\n7. Keep the learned rules in the new model and audit final state. O9 is useful recoverability, but its old 'every changed path' approval language does not specify the new branch-rule model or reviewer-author exclusions. Define what can be checked at activation and how admin recovery works after later membership changes; an unreachable guarantee must not become a blocking gate. O14's keyboard/focus and no-page-write-credential rules are useful browser outcomes; assign them explicitly to R2/IA/I5 without restoring old UI suites. The removal audit's meanings/export/module/config/resource/request checks are useful; distinguish current identified Artroom resources and authoritative E1 settlement evidence from an unbounded ownership sweep or a search-only proof. Stop/fence writers before census and preserve needed late-outcome readers. Historical evidence and closed old tasks are retained, not automatically rewritten, replayed or satisfied. Production rollout and excluded tooling remain outside commissioning.\n\nAdditional current records have been read in full: checker42545b0c requests one source-qualified P2 carry-evidence boundary repair atd691 under the normal intermediate-release binding, without rerunning the rejected private diagnostic; its causal-staleness is recorded, not treated as approval. Builder27b2fa7e announces R3rev3 and asks for new check-error job states/staging/register contracts. Builder9fa55f9b asks the normal same-subject live-basis R0 verdict refresh before adoption, preservingunchanged frozen bytes. Source fix/landing coordination remains with the sprint owner; R4 stays unfiled as recorded. No competing source instructions, review override, new gate, tests, builds, installs, provider actions or deployment were performed/commissioned by this planning reading.","body":{"head":"2f83bf8c75c7fec706cd2310eeef5c986da0e2bb","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Complete R4 main/catalogue and explicitly bounded sample readings; remaining full three-audit reading owed."}}